      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOGAN DOWNS (1) has recently joined the Matt Hoysted stable, and he finished fourth when making his debut as the favourite at Newcastle, and will be a lot stronger now. A recent trial win will ensure that he is ready to rumble fresh, especially from the pole position. On top. QUANTUM OVERDRIVE (2) was put aside after a modest debut run at Ipswich in January, and he resumes with a couple of solid trials under his belt. The Archibald stable seldom trek to this course unless they are confident, so follow the market in. EGYPTIAN GODDESS (6) resumed with a game effort for second at Beaudesert nearly 3 weeks ago, and she strips fitter for this. Ash Butler sticks with her, and so do we. MISHANI SENORITA (8) has raced her way into some good form, and around this tight track from a good draw, she can figure in the top 4 again. LEGAS SPIRIT (3) make her debut off the back of a fair Doomben trial. Justin P Stanley is always a positive booking, and she is worth including.",
